From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 23:38:37 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] [CUDA] Support SM120 kind::mxf8f6f4 block-scaled MMA

Add the MX block-scaled warp MMA of the SM120 family (SM120, SM121/GB10):
mma.sync.m16n8k32.kind::mxf8f6f4.block_scale.scale_vec::1X with UE8M0
scales, one per 32 K elements, for E4M3/E5M2 and E2M1 operands, in any
combination. T.gemm_blockscaled / T.mma_gemm_blockscaled pick the kind from
the operand dtypes: packed E2M1 on both sides keeps kind::mxf4nvf4, and
anything else lowers to kind::mxf8f6f4.

Scales use the existing packed uint32 words: one word holds the scales of
four consecutive K32 atoms, and the emitter passes the byte selector, which
folds to a constant when the K tile is a multiple of 128.

E2M1 operands come from float4_e2m1_unpacked shared memory, the TMA
16U4_ALIGN16B layout TileLang already uses for tcgen05 f8f6f4. A new
tl.ptx_ldmatrix variant, ldmatrix.m8n16.b8x16.b4x16_p64, expands those
padded rows into 8-bit containers and shifts E2M1 into bits [5:2], where
kind::f8f6f4/mxf8f6f4 reads it. Register fragments of unpacked FP4 are uint8.

The compact K-major scale package and the static four-block ping-pong stay
NVF4-only; kind::mxf8f6f4 uses row-major scale words and A in shared memory.
A register-fragment A is rejected: on SM121 a plain FP8 T.gemm with fragment
A also gives wrong results, so the generic 8-bit fragment layout needs its own
fix first.

Validated on GB10 (sm_121a, CUDA 13.0.2): the block-scaled suites pass (206
tests), including exact E4M3 x E4M3 and E4M3 x E2M1 products.
